      "raw_text": "To find the percentage of time Carol spent editing, we need to determine the total time spent on all tasks and then calculate the ratio of the editing time to that total.\n\n**Step 1: Convert all time measurements to the same unit.**\nThe problem provides times in hours and minutes. It is easiest to convert everything to minutes.\n*   **Writing time:** 4 hours.\n    Since 1 hour = 60 minutes:\n    $4 \\times 60 = 240$ minutes.\n*   **Recording time:** Half the time spent writing.\n    $240 / 2 = 120$ minutes.\n*   **Editing time:** 90 minutes (already in minutes).\n\n**Step 2: Calculate the total work time.**\nAdd the time spent on writing, recording, and editing:\n$$ \\text{Total Time} = \\text{Writing} + \\text{Recording} + \\text{Editing} $$\n$$ \\text{Total Time} = 240 + 120 + 90 $$\n$$ \\text{Total Time} = 450 \\text{ minutes} $$\n\n**Step 3: Calculate the percentage of time spent editing.**\nThe formula for percentage is:\n$$ \\text{Percentage} = \\left( \\frac{\\text{Part}}{\\text{Whole}} \\right) \\times 100 $$\nHere, the \"Part\" is the editing time (90 minutes) and the \"Whole\" is the total time (450 minutes).\n\n$$ \\text{Percentage} = \\left( \\frac{90}{450} \\right) \\times 100 $$\n\nSimplify the fraction:\n$$ \\frac{90}{450} = \\frac{9}{45} = \\frac{1}{5} $$\n\nConvert to percentage:\n$$ \\frac{1}{5} \\times 100 = 20\\% $$\n\nCarol spent 20% of her total work time editing.\n\n#### 20%<|im_end|>",
      "answer_text": "To find the percentage of time Carol spent editing, we need to determine the total time spent on all tasks and then calculate the ratio of the editing time to that total.\n\n**Step 1: Convert all time measurements to the same unit.**\nThe problem provides times in hours and minutes. It is easiest to convert everything to minutes.\n*   **Writing time:** 4 hours.\n    Since 1 hour = 60 minutes:\n    $4 \\times 60 = 240$ minutes.\n*   **Recording time:** Half the time spent writing.\n    $240 / 2 = 120$ minutes.\n*   **Editing time:** 90 minutes (already in minutes).\n\n**Step 2: Calculate the total work time.**\nAdd the time spent on writing, recording, and editing:\n$$ \\text{Total Time} = \\text{Writing} + \\text{Recording} + \\text{Editing} $$\n$$ \\text{Total Time} = 240 + 120 + 90 $$\n$$ \\text{Total Time} = 450 \\text{ minutes} $$\n\n**Step 3: Calculate the percentage of time spent editing.**\nThe formula for percentage is:\n$$ \\text{Percentage} = \\left( \\frac{\\text{Part}}{\\text{Whole}} \\right) \\times 100 $$\nHere, the \"Part\" is the editing time (90 minutes) and the \"Whole\" is the total time (450 minutes).\n\n$$ \\text{Percentage} = \\left( \\frac{90}{450} \\right) \\times 100 $$\n\nSimplify the fraction:\n$$ \\frac{90}{450} = \\frac{9}{45} = \\frac{1}{5} $$\n\nConvert to percentage:\n$$ \\frac{1}{5} \\times 100 = 20\\% $$\n\nCarol spent 20% of her total work time editing.\n\n#### 20%",
